Nantes-based startup GreenRoute, which develops route-planning software for delivery companies, has raised €5 million from a group of investors. The software calculates the most fuel-efficient routes for delivery vans, {{1}} customers to cut fuel costs by up to 15 percent.

The company plans to use the funds to {{2}} its engineering team and to enter the German market. {{3}}

Founded in 2021 by two former logistics managers, GreenRoute now works with more than 300 clients. Co-founder Léa Garnier says the company {{4}} profitable by the end of next year.
